Z||000000||Vlad||10-10-2000||12:06 AM||||Hello guys<P>What I have is a wierd clicking noise coming from throttle body once or twice a day while slowly accelerating from zero. The frequency of clicking is very high. 2 or 3 clicks per second. Also, there is a vibration of the gas pedal while it's clicking at the back.<P>The noise usually goes away if I either complitely release a gas pedal or floor it.<P>In additional, (could be related) the gas pedal is sort of sticking. This is not  cables. WD40 on the return spring of throttle body and some not very deep cleaning didn't help much.<P>Thanks in advance.<P>85 GT V6<p>[This message has been edited by Vlad (edited 10-10-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||10-10-2000||04:48 AM||||Are you certain that your cable isn't kinked anywhere? also, just a thought, had a car once (non-fiero) where I didn't have the timing quite right, and it would backfire just slightly back through the carb, and gave a "popping" feel in the accelerator pedel....but It was obvious it wasn't running quite right either, which I assume this isn't the case. It also might be possible that some of the linkage, (if a 4-banger)or throttle shaft is bent causing a bind somewhere. Just a few thoughts.||||reg||1
